{
  "version": "Notebook/1.0",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## Coverage\nThis workbook has been created to provide a consolidated view of coverage for Defender for Cloud plans and offerings across all selected subscriptions and multi-cloud connectors.\n\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 19 19\" width=\"20\" class=\"fxt-escapeShadow\" role=\"presentation\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns:svg=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><g><path fill=\"#1b93eb\" d=\"M16.82 8.886c0 4.81-5.752 8.574-7.006 9.411a.477.477 0 01-.523 0C8.036 17.565 2.18 13.7 2.18 8.886V3.135a.451.451 0 01.42-.419C7.2 2.612 6.154.625 9.5.625s2.3 1.987 6.8 2.091a.479.479 0 01.523.419z\"></path><path fill=\"url(#0024423711759027356)\" d=\"M16.192 8.99c0 4.392-5.333 7.947-6.483 8.575a.319.319 0 01-.418 0c-1.15-.732-6.483-4.183-6.483-8.575V3.762a.575.575 0 01.313-.523C7.2 3.135 6.258 1.357 9.4 1.357s2.2 1.882 6.274 1.882a.45.45 0 01.419.418z\"></path><path d=\"M9.219 5.378a.313.313 0 01.562 0l.875 1.772a.314.314 0 00.236.172l1.957.284a.314.314 0 01.174.535l-1.416 1.38a.312.312 0 00-.09.278l.334 1.949a.313.313 0 01-.455.33l-1.75-.92a.314.314 0 00-.292 0l-1.75.92a.313.313 0 01-.455-.33L7.483 9.8a.312.312 0 00-.09-.278L5.977 8.141a.314.314 0 01.174-.535l1.957-.284a.314.314 0 00.236-.172z\" class=\"msportalfx-svg-c01\"></path></g></svg>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Open Sans; font-weight: 620; font-size: 14px;font-style: bold;margin:-10px 0px 0px 0px;position: relative;top:-3px;left:-4px;\"> Please take the time to answer a quick survey. To submit your feedback,\n</span>[<span style=\"font-family: Open Sans; font-weight: 620; font-size: 14px;font-style: bold;margin:-10px 0px 0px 0px;position: relative;top:-3px;left:-4px;\"> click here. </span>](https://aka.ms/mdfcsurveycoverageworkbook)"
      },
      "name": "Defender for Cloud Coverage"
    },
    {
      "type": 9,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "id": "7a8be0a4-2557-43c9-afb5-9e3c9fdc11f7",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "Subscriptions",
            "type": 6,
            "isRequired": true,
            "multiSelect": true,
            "quote": "'",
            "delimiter": ",",
            "value": [
              "value::all"
            ],
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": [
                "value::all"
              ],
              "includeAll": true,
              "showDefault": false
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "d4e04df2-4d8b-4127-b769-de821c7895db",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "info",
            "label": "Additional information",
            "type": 10,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": "Off",
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": []
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n { \"value\": \"On\", \"label\": \"On\"},\n { \"value\": \"Off\", \"label\": \"Off\"}\n]",
            "timeContext": {
              "durationMs": 86400000
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "f22a92ae-4573-499f-8921-8857be250f14",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "relativeCoverage",
            "label": "Relative coverage",
            "type": 10,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": []
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n { \"value\": \"Yes\", \"label\": \"Yes\"},\n { \"value\": \"No\", \"label\": \"No\"}\n]",
            "timeContext": {
              "durationMs": 86400000
            },
            "value": "Yes"
          },
          {
            "id": "49faad8a-8c99-4343-b11b-be188eb082a6",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "absoluteCoverage",
            "type": 10,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": []
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n { \"value\": \"Yes\", \"label\": \"Yes\"},\n { \"value\": \"No\", \"label\": \"No\"}\n]",
            "timeContext": {
              "durationMs": 86400000
            },
            "value": "Yes",
            "label": "Absolute coverage"
          },
          {
            "id": "d5c581af-3a66-401b-8862-dc2950449389",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "detailedCoverage",
            "label": "Detailed coverage",
            "type": 10,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": []
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n { \"value\": \"Yes\", \"label\": \"Yes\"},\n { \"value\": \"No\", \"label\": \"No\"}\n]",
            "timeContext": {
              "durationMs": 86400000
            },
            "value": "Yes"
          }
        ],
        "style": "above",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces"
      },
      "name": "info"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "Use the different filter options above to show relative, absolute, and detailed coverage for your environment.\n\n- **Relative coverage** shows the percentage of subscriptions/connectors that have a particular Defender for Cloud plan enabled.\n- **Absolute coverage** shows each plan's status per subscription.\n- The **detailed coverage** section has been added to show additional settings that can/need to be enabled on relevant plans in order to get each plan's full value.\n\n**Azure Defender CSPM components:** After Subscription Name, the component columns appear left to right in the same order as the top-to-bottom Defender CSPM settings list:\n\n1. Agentless scanning for machines\n2. Kubernetes API access\n3. Registry access\n4. Sensitive data discovery\n5. Cloud Infrastructure and Entitlements Management (CIEM)\n6. API Security Posture Management\n7. Serverless protection\n8. Serverless containers\n\n**Enabled** and **Disabled** reflect the reported component setting. **Not reported** means the setting is missing, empty, or unrecognized in Azure Resource Graph; it must not be interpreted as disabled. These are configuration states, not confirmation of successful scanning or resource-level protection. Serverless containers require Registry access for full coverage. See [Defender CSPM components](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/tutorial-enable-cspm-plan#enable-the-components-of-the-defender-cspm-plan).\n\nFor Defender for AI Services, detailed coverage reports suspicious prompt evidence and AI Model Security (Preview) component settings. Not reported means a component setting was absent or unrecognized, not necessarily disabled. Component configuration does not establish that models were scanned.\n\n**Portal-aligned detailed coverage:** AWS and GCP columns follow the sampled Defender for Cloud settings order; existing data-aware database posture fields remain after the portal settings. In the updated Azure Servers and Containers and AWS/GCP detailed views, missing or unrecognized settings are **Not reported**, not Disabled. CIEM is Not reported when no explicit enabled value is available; configuration-object presence alone does not establish its state. Some portal settings, including CloudTrail and Cloud Logging ingestion, Azure Policy and agent provisioning settings, do not have a verified Resource Graph enabled field and are not listed as coverage.\n\n**Defender for Storage:** Detailed coverage includes only subscriptions using the `DefenderForStorageV2` sub-plan; other Storage pricing options remain included in overall coverage.\n\n**Defender for Storage:** The detailed table includes the configured subscription plan, malware scanning state, per-account monthly scanning cap in GB, and sensitive data discovery. The cap field is already expressed in GB/month/account; -1 means unlimited and missing or unrecognized values are Not reported. Storage-account overrides can differ from subscription settings. The separate Activity monitoring table samples seven days of Blob and File transactions and filtered Blob upload ingress, projects them to 30 days, and models malware scanning as the smaller of uploaded GB and the scenario cap entered for the selected accounts. It does not read the configured cap into that scenario automatically and is not a measured scan volume. Multiple scans, unscannable blobs, and missing metrics can make the model differ from actual scanned volume. An incomplete metrics status means values must not be interpreted as a complete activity total. [Storage plan configuration](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/defender-for-storage-powershell-enablement).\n\n**Defender for APIs:** Detailed coverage shows the subscription-level plan status and configured plan reported by Azure Resource Graph. A missing or unrecognized status or a missing plan is Not reported; a disabled plan is Not applicable. Subscriptions without an API pricing resource are not shown. An enabled subscription plan does not confirm that individual APIs are onboarded or protected."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "info",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "On"
      },
      "name": "infoText"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## Release notes\n\n|Version|Description|Date|\n|---|---|---|\n| v1.0 | initial release, public availability of Defender for Cloud Coverage Workbook | January 20, 2022 |\n| v1.1 | adding navigation menu and coverage for AWS connectors | February 21, 2022 |\n| v1.2 | Updating AWS query and adding coverage for GCP connectors after API update | March 23, 2022|\n| v1.3 | adding Defender for Servers P1/P2 | April 7, 2022 |\n| v1.4 | adding relative coverage | April 14, 2022 |\n| v1.5 | adding coverage for Defender for Databases on multicloud connectors | June 27, 2022|\n| v1.6 | adding coverage for Defender CSPM | October 12, 2022 |\n| v1.7 | adding information about Defender for Storage pricing tier | February 28, 2023 |\n| v1.8 | updating queries for business model changes in Defender for Resource Manager, DNS, Key Vault | July 31, 2023|\n| v1.9 | adding detailed coverage for relevant plans' extensions | September 08, 2023|\n| v1.10 | adding detailed coverage for multicloud connectors | November 08, 2023|\n| v1.11 | adding Azure CSPM API posture, Serverless protection, and Serverless containers settings; distinguishing unreported settings from disabled components | October 28, 2026|\n| v1.12 | adding Defender for AI Services plan and detailed component coverage | November 23, 2026 |\n| v1.13 | aligning Azure, AWS and GCP detailed coverage with portal settings; adding supported container, serverless and database components; updating Defender for Storage labels | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.14 | adding Defender for Storage plan, monthly scanning cap, and non-cost activity monitoring | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.15 | adding detailed Defender for APIs status and configured plan | November 24, 2026 |"
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "info",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "On"
      },
      "name": "releaseNotes"
    },
    {
      "type": 11,
      "content": {
